# FIGURE INTEGRATION PROTOCOL

**CRITICAL**: Imaging chapters require MAXIMUM figure density.

**Density Target**: 1 figure per 100-150 words (higher than other chapter types)
- Imaging content is inherently visual — every finding needs illustration

**Figure Placement Rules**:
1. EVERY imaging finding described must have `[FIGURE: <id>]`
2. EVERY sequence/protocol comparison needs side-by-side figures
3. EVERY differential diagnosis needs comparative figure examples
4. EVERY measurement criterion needs annotated figure

**Figure Type Mapping for Imaging Chapters**:

| Content Type | Required Figure Types |
|--------------|----------------------|
| Protocol description | Protocol diagram, sequence comparison |
| Signal characteristics | Annotated MRI showing signal on each sequence |
| Density characteristics | CT windows showing lesion appearance |
| Enhancement pattern | Pre/post contrast comparison |
| Differential diagnosis | Side-by-side comparison of mimics |
| Anatomical correlation | Imaging-anatomy overlay |
| Measurement criteria | Annotated measurement example |

---

# CITATION FORMAT

Use XML citation anchoring: `<cite source="SOURCE_ID"/>`

**Citation Requirements**:
- Sensitivity/specificity values require citation
- Protocol recommendations require citation
- Diagnostic criteria require citation
- Measurement thresholds require citation

